{
  "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
  "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nERIC E. MURPHY, State Solicitor, Columbus, Ohio; on behalf of the Petitioners and the State Respondents in support.\nMALCOLM L. STEWART, Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent United States, in support of the Petitioners.\nEVAN R. CHESLER, ESQ., New York, New York; on behalf of the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Eric E. Murphy",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The government met its initial burden to show anticompetitive harm in this case under the rule of reason by proving that American Express's anti-steering provisions have stifled interbrand price competition and raised the prices that all four credit card companies charge merchants."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: We're not here to protect competitors, right, Mr. Murphy?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: And that's normally what the antitrust laws care about, is deadweight loss. That's the primary concern of antitrust activity, wouldn't you agree?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Isn't that true, given American Express's tying or -- or restriction that no merchant can offer a consumer a 5 or 10 or other discount for using Visa, MasterCard, or Discover, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Does output include premiums to -- or rewards to customers?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Malcolm L. Stewart",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The purpose and effect of Amex's anti-steering rules is to eliminate price competition across an entire market. Yet the Second Circuit held that the plaintiffs had not even established a prima facie case of anticompetitive effect."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Malcolm L. Stewart",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0000-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Circuit erred by conflating the question, have reward -- have cardholder rewards become more generous, with the appropriate question, has competition on the cardholder side been enhanced?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We do the same thing, don't we, with nuts and bolts? We give the people nuts and we give them bolts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stewart",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And our point about the cardholder side is that the Second Circuit may have been right when it said the effect of this -- the anti-steering rules was that, on the whole, cardholder benefits may have become more generous."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stewart",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Court should proceed cautiously about announcing categorical rules and can say that, for purposes of this case, it is sufficient to -- the fact that there is four-way competition on the merchant side and thousands-way competition on the cardholder side is by itself a sufficient ground for treating these as distinct markets."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And they're free to do that, right? I mean, American Express's agreements don't affect MasterCard or Visa's opportunity to cut their fees, their own fees, or to advertise that American Express's are higher."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Absent a horizontal agreement, we have that, don't we?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Chesler",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The district court described competition for credit card transactions as fierce. There is no transaction without a cardholder and a merchant simultaneously executing one. To compete for that business against ubiquitous and, frankly, larger rivals, Amex offers consumers what they want, and transaction volume has, in fact, increased dramatically and accordingly."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Isn't that the essence of competition, to have somebody working against you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You haven't told me why it doesn't remove competition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Chesler",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CHESLER: And what I'm here to tell you is, with respect to the product at issue here, which is credit card transactions, the government did not prove that there was an anticompetitive effect because output was up, quality was up, and they didn't prove what the price of that product was."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What -- what's the vertical case? Even Leegin didn't say that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Chesler",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the result that we're trying to avoid here is a situation in which a plaintiff can fail to prove what the price of the product is, merely that there's been an increase to part of that price, and that that's enough to satisfy the first leg of the rule of reason."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Chesler",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government had failed to prove what the costs were for the -- for the services provided to the merchant, and it failed to prove what the -- what the consumer's side of the price was."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0003-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the most important point for this Court to take from this case is that certainly the Court has lessened the scrutiny with respect to vertical restraints in recent -- recent years, but this particular vertical restraint, the one at issue here, has the same effects that we would anticipate happening with a horizontal cartel."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "what is the relief that you're seeking? Are you seeking to say the Second Circuit was wrong in saying you didn't -- the government didn't prove step 1, and now he goes back for a step 2 examination?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "whether the government met its prima facie case based on the effects that we showed at the trial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "District Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the district court found as a fact that higher prices weren't rising because of the cardholder rewards. They were rising because of these restraints."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I -- I just want to pause right there. You -- you accept that to show an anticompetitive effect, you have to show not just an agreement"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ed895508f34fd62a5a8e3ec666fa26d46100593e95e30c3df99d2489fa055209",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed895508f34f-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "we showed market power, but we showed it quite powerfully in this case with this restraint affecting merchants making up some 90 percent of the market."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1454",
      "confidence": 0.0,
